---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import SocialLinks from '../components/SocialLinks.astro';
import DashedLine from '../components/DashedLine.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="关于 — ChrisV">
  <SectionHeader tag="ABOUT" title="关于我" />

  <section class="container-inner pb-16">
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 text-center">
      <img
        src="/images/logo.jpg"
        alt="ChrisV avatar"
        width="96"
        height="96"
        class="h-24 w-24 rounded-full object-cover"
      />
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-[var(--color-0)]">ChrisV</h2>
      <SocialLinks class="justify-center" />

      <div
        class="max-w-[520px] space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-300)] text-balance"
      >
        <p>我是一名传统工科的硕士研究生，但心思常常不在同一处。</p>
        <p>
          白天算偏微分方程、算有限元、做学校的科研项目，晚上读论文、写代码、调模型。我着迷于把一件事的逻辑拆干净，也着迷于让呈现方式好看优雅一点。AI、Agent、NLP
          是我探索世界的工具，设计和艺术是我理解自己的方式。
        </p>
        <p>
          这个博客是我的工作台，也是我的草稿纸。这里会放我读过的论文、做过的项目、突然冒出来的念头。我不确定最后会走到哪里，但我很享受这种一边建造一边思考的状态。
        </p>
        <p>
          如果你也对智能系统和美学之间的缝隙感兴趣，欢迎在这里随便逛逛。
        </p>
      </div>

      <DashedLine class="max-w-[120px]" />

      <div
        class="max-w-[520px] space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-300)] text-balance"
      >
        <p>
          I am a master's student in traditional engineering, though my mind
          rarely stays in one place.
        </p>
        <p>
          By day I solve partial differential equations, run finite element
          analysis, and work on my university research projects; by night I read
          papers, write code, and tune models. I am obsessed with taking things
          apart until the logic is clean, and just as obsessed with making the
          presentation beautiful and elegant. AI, agents, and NLP are my tools
          for exploring the world; design and art are how I understand myself.
        </p>
        <p>
          This blog is my workbench and my scratch paper. Here I keep papers I
          have read, projects I have built, and ideas that pop up out of nowhere.
          I am not sure where all of this will lead, but I enjoy the state of
          building and thinking at the same time.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you too are interested in the space between intelligent systems and
          aesthetics, feel free to wander around.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
